  "hooks": [
    "Alma trades the judgment seat for the pulpit (4:19–20). Nephi makes the same move in Helaman 5:1.",
    "Chapters 17–26 rewind fourteen years: the sons of Mosiah's mission runs alongside Alma 1–16.",
    "The people of Ammon bury their swords; their sons take them up — and none of the 2,000 die (57:25).",
    "Alma 32–34 is one argument in three voices: faith as a seed, Zenos on prayer, Amulek on the Atonement.",
    "Alma doesn't die on the page. He departs, and is thought buried by the Lord, like Moses (45:19)."
  ]
